<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hlukhiv</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Glukhov</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hlukhiv is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumy">Sumy</a> Oblast in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>. First mentioned in 1152 in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chernigov">Chernigov</a> lands, it was the seat of a small principality of the Olgovichi, from which the princes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/novosil">Novosil</a> and the Upper Oka descended. From 1708 to 1764 it was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossack-hetmanate">Cossack Hetmanate</a> and the seat of the Little Russian Collegium.</p></div>
